  "blocks": [
    {
      "block_id": 0,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "_\nSection 3.1\nee\n_\nDesigning Hardware for the Amiga Expansion\nArchitecture\n|\n",
      "bbox": [
        11.039993286132812,
        48.719970703125,
        540.3936157226562,
        128.41964721679688
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.020390058430024373,
        0.06759902969747658,
        0.9980674004247345,
        0.17818244593876362
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 1,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "INTRODUCTION\nThis section gives guidelines for designing hardware to reside on the\n~\n",
      "bbox": [
        10.79998779296875,
        170.87994384765625,
        502.968017578125,
        189.60140991210938
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.019946785875204164,
        0.2370961688226122,
        0.9289450637377968,
        0.2630722300190138
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 2,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "_\nAmiga expansion bus. The Amiga expansion bus is a relatively\nstraightforward extension of the 68000 bus.\n",
      "bbox": [
        192.95999145507812,
        183.5999755859375,
        474.3117980957031,
        208.33193969726562
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.3563829613345939,
        0.2547452312259639,
        0.8760191266936033,
        0.28906086714097806
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 3,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "_\nHardware for the bus can be viewed as two categories: backplanes\nand PICs. Backplanes interface to the 86 pin connector of either\n",
      "bbox": [
        10.32000732421875,
        219.3599853515625,
        498.5278015136719,
        244.09268188476562
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.019060297129293774,
        0.3043622964097384,
        0.9207443101096353,
        0.3386789485611617
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 4,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "oo\nanother backplane or the Amiga itself. Backplanes buffer the bus and\n",
      "bbox": [
        70.32000732421875,
        243.11996459960938,
        503.166015625,
        258.7211608886719
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.12987589946649475,
        0.3373293019234984,
        0.9293107516182308,
        0.35897598430117994
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 5,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "~\nprovide 100 pin connectors for PICs to plug into.\nI\nls\nPIC is an acronym for plug-in card. A PIC is usually a card that plugs\ninto the standard 100 pin Amiga connectors.\n",
      "bbox": [
        10.079977035522461,
        256.0799560546875,
        503.9039611816406,
        303.37005615234375
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.018616978778942916,
        0.3553113087803842,
        0.930673682974084,
        0.4209263909481791
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 6,
      "type": 0,
      "text": ".\nA sub-type of PIC is a combination of backplane and PIC integrated\ninto one package. These combination products should follow all of\n—\nthe applicable backplane and PIC rules, especially auto-configuration.\n",
      "bbox": [
        10.079986572265625,
        315.3599853515625,
        504.407958984375,
        353.7743835449219
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.01861699639260855,
        0.4375624350243846,
        0.931604529975528,
        0.4908624679843188
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 7,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "Software never sees backplanes; all expansion hardware appears to\n",
      "bbox": [
        208.32000732421875,
        364.7999572753906,
        502.2647705078125,
        376.57171630859375
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.38475178484205697,
        0.5061604674551984,
        0.9276462179429876,
        0.5224938001110407
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 8,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "_\nthe software as PICs.\n",
      "bbox": [
        10.079986572265625,
        378.2399597167969,
        300.1200256347656,
        394.5628356933594
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.01861699639260855,
        0.5248084902487036,
        0.5542996902362125,
        0.5474565042348265
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 9,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "_\n",
      "bbox": [
        10.79998779296875,
        432.9599609375,
        19.195201873779297,
        434.4013977050781
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.019946785875204164,
        0.6007325709527792,
        0.035452130960450357,
        0.6027325665490881
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 10,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "WARNING\n",
      "bbox": [
        333.1199951171875,
        417.1199645996094,
        380.4539489746094,
        425.5283508300781
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.615248215157943,
        0.5787545531625446,
        0.7026705586198011,
        0.5904212011982105
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 11,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "These specifications represent “worst case” design targets.\n",
      "bbox": [
        217.67999267578125,
        440.6399841308594,
        474.8832092285156,
        452.8922119140625
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.4020389917520699,
        0.6113886142227706,
        0.8770744811746832,
        0.628388597962988
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 12,
      "type": 0,
      "text": ",\nProducts that do not comply with these specifications can be ex-\n~\npected to fail on worst case production units.\n",
      "bbox": [
        10.79998779296875,
        452.15997314453125,
        496.74005126953125,
        476.6519470214844
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.019946785875204164,
        0.627372615612982,
        0.9174424664407533,
        0.6613552647312783
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 13,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "Following conservative design practices and allowing the widest\n",
      "bbox": [
        218.39999389648438,
        487.4399719238281,
        484.1760559082031,
        500.4129333496094
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.4033687812346655,
        0.6763236648601371,
        0.8942376878786304,
        0.6943236675701009
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 14,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "_\nsafety margins is your best assurance against problems in the\nfield.\n",
      "bbox": [
        11.040008544921875,
        499.6799621582031,
